            "pages": {
              "end": 9,
              "start": 9
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Srinivasan, the case concerns whether a person who uses a telephone to purchase drugs for personal use falls within the scope of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u202f843(b)."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Srinivasan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0a9a0c68880603e24fca1c19c16a4838ba670ca9f19ffdee4a3925eede71c8ae",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0a9a0c688806-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 9,
              "start": 9
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Srinivasan, the petitioner argues that the buyer/seller principle excludes buyers from liability under the statute."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0a9a0c68880603e24fca1c19c16a4838ba670ca9f19ffdee4a3925eede71c8ae",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0a9a0c688806-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The government argues that such conduct should be covered by the statute by treating it as facilitating the dealer's felony."
      }
    ],
